message: If you use BlaBla or its benchmark artifacts, please cite this repository.
title: "BlaBla: executable project memory for coding agents"
type: software
version: 0.9.0
date-released: 2026-09-24
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kiborgik/blabla"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22761364
    description: Concept DOI resolving to the latest archived version
authors:
  - family-names: Yakovyshyn
    given-names: Petro
abstract: >-
  BlaBla moves project intent out of chat context and into the repository, where
  coding agents can query and verify it. Behavior and Structure contracts are
  executable and decide completion through a GREEN/YELLOW/RED gate; Mission,
  System, Process and Knowledge memory is queryable and advisory. A coverage-guided
  behavior verifier produces minimized counterexamples, a static structure verifier
  runs language providers, and bounded task records with a deterministic challenge
  command carry scope, deliverables and findings across agent handoffs. The
  repository includes a four-stage fresh-context handoff benchmark with its
  methodology, prompts, scorers and results.
keywords:
  - coding-agents
  - verification
  - property-based-testing
  - executable-specification
  - llm
